course: dictionary
lesson: 2328
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word crown can mean a round ornament for a king or queen, the top part of something, or a cover for a damaged tooth. To find the right meaning, read the context: the words around it are your clues.
explain: «The red-crowned crane stands about 1.5 metres tall.» The clues say the red patch is on its head, so here crown means the top part of the head. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Crown can also be a verb. «Charles was crowned king» means someone had a crown put on them to make them king. The ending -ed tells you it happened in the past.
fact: Crown is a noun for a round ornament, often gold with jewels, that a king or queen wears on the head.
fact: The Crown, with a capital C, can mean the power of the king or queen and the government.
fact: Crown can also mean the top part of something, like your head, a hat, a tree or a tooth.
fact: A crown is also a cover a dentist puts on a damaged tooth.
fact: To crown someone means to put a crown on them to make them king or queen, or to declare them a winner.
exercise: «The red-crowned crane stands about 1.5 metres tall.» In this sentence, what does crown mean? | A prize for the winner | A round gold ornament for a king | A cover for a damaged tooth | *The top part of the head
exercise: «Charles was crowned king at Westminster Abbey.» What does crowned mean here? | Had a cover put on a tooth | *Had a crown put on him to make him king | Had the top cut off | Was given a prize for running fast
exercise: The dentist put a crown on Ella's back tooth. What is a crown here? | A winner's medal | *A cover that goes over a damaged tooth | A round gold ornament for a king | The top of a tree
test: In the phrase «the crown of the head», what does crown mean? | A cover for a tooth | *The top part of something | To put someone in charge | A gold ornament with jewels
test: Sam wins the race and his teacher says, «We crown you champion!» What does crown mean? | To cut the top off something | *To declare someone a winner | To sign a treaty | To wear a gold ornament
exam: In «In 1840 the British Crown signed the Treaty of Waitangi», what does Crown mean? | A cover for a damaged tooth | *The power of the king or queen and the government | A round gold ornament for the head | The top part of a tree
